# Proxy Detector — Face Recognition + GPS Attendance Fraud Detection

A full-stack attendance system that flags proxy attendance attempts by
independently verifying two signals before accepting a check-in: the
student's face (matched against a one-time enrollment) and their live GPS
location (checked against a campus geofence). Either check failing doesn't
silently block the request — it logs a flagged record so faculty/admins get
a full audit trail of who attempted to mark attendance, when, and why it
was rejected.

## Why this exists

Manual or roll-call attendance is easy to fake — a friend can mark for you,
or you can mark from outside campus. This project replaces that with two
independent, hard-to-fake signals checked server-side on every attempt.

## Tech stack

- **Frontend:** React (Vite), face-api.js for in-browser face detection/recognition, React Router
- **Backend:** Node.js, Express, JWT auth
- **Database:** MongoDB (Mongoose)
- **Face recognition:** face-api.js (TinyFaceDetector + FaceLandmark68 + FaceRecognitionNet) running entirely client-side — only a 128-length numeric descriptor is ever sent to the server, never raw images
- **Geofencing:** Haversine distance formula comparing live GPS coordinates against a configured campus center point and radius

## How it works

1. **Enrollment (once, at registration):** the student's webcam captures a
   face descriptor (a 128-dimension vector representing facial geometry)
   using face-api.js, which is stored against their account.
2. **Marking attendance:** the student opens the camera again. The app
   captures a live face descriptor and the device's GPS coordinates at the
   same time.
3. **Server-side verification:**
   - *Face check* — Euclidean distance between the live descriptor and the
     enrolled one. Below a configurable threshold (default `0.55`) counts
     as a match.
   - *Location check* — Haversine distance between the live GPS point and
     the configured campus center. Inside the configured radius (default
     `300m`) counts as within-bounds.
   - If both pass, attendance is marked **present**. If either fails, it's
     stored as **flagged** with the specific reason (`face_mismatch`,
     `outside_geofence`, or both), instead of being silently rejected.
4. **Dashboards:** students see their own attendance history; admins see
   every record, can filter by status, and see daily/all-time flagged
   counts.

## Project structure

```
proxy-detector/
├── backend/
│   ├── server.js
│   ├── config/db.js
│   ├── models/          # User, Attendance
│   ├── controllers/      # auth, attendance, admin
│   ├── routes/
│   ├── middleware/        # JWT auth + role guard
│   └── utils/             # geoUtils (haversine), faceUtils (euclidean distance)
└── frontend/
    ├── src/
    │   ├── pages/         # Login, Register, MarkAttendance, Dashboard, AdminDashboard
    │   ├── components/
    │   ├── context/        # AuthContext
    │   ├── utils/faceapi.js
    │   └── api/axios.js
    └── public/models/      # face-api.js model weights (see README inside)
```

## Running it locally

### Backend
```bash
cd backend
npm install
cp .env.example .env   # fill in MONGO_URI, JWT_SECRET, campus lat/lng/radius
npm run dev
```

### Frontend
```bash
cd frontend
npm install
cp .env.example .env
# download face-api.js model weights — see public/models/README.md
npm run dev
```

The app expects MongoDB running locally or a connection string to MongoDB
Atlas. Set `CAMPUS_LAT`, `CAMPUS_LNG`, and `CAMPUS_RADIUS_METERS` in the
backend `.env` to your actual campus/classroom coordinates.

## Possible future improvements

- Liveness detection to prevent a photo/video being held up to the camera
- Admin-configurable geofence (currently set via env vars)
- Per-class schedules instead of a single daily mark
- Push/email alert to faculty the moment a flagged attempt is logged
